---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Journal" description="Reporting and commentary on AI-made films, the tools behind them, and where the festival and awards world is heading.">
  <h1 style="margin-top:34px">Journal</h1>
  <p class="lede" style="color:var(--muted); max-width:640px; line-height:1.6; margin-bottom:34px;">Reporting and commentary on AI-made films, the tools behind them, and where the festival and awards world is heading.</p>

  <article style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr; gap:32px; align-items:center; margin:0 0 44px; padding-bottom:40px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);">
    <div style="border-radius:10px; overflow:hidden; aspect-ratio:16/9; background:var(--bg-elev); display:block;">
      <img src="/images/posters/reset-wide.webp" alt="RESET title card" style="width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover; display:block;" />
    </div>
    <div>
      <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; margin-bottom:10px; font-size:.78rem; color:var(--muted);">
        <span style="display:inline-flex; align-items:center; background:var(--bg-elev); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:999px; padding:3px 11px; font-size:.68rem; font-weight:700; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.04em;">Editorial</span>
        <time datetime="2026-09-22">Sep 22, 2026</time>
      </div>
      <h2 style="font-size:1.7rem; line-height:1.15; margin:0 0 .4em;">RESET makes the case for the one-person AI film crew</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--muted); line-height:1.6; margin:0;">Max Barskih's RESET — written, directed, and entirely produced solo using Higgsfield AI — is the clearest sign yet that a single filmmaker can now credibly deliver a multi-location sci-fi short without a crew. Its selection at the Higgsfield Global Film Festival says less about novelty and more about craft: the lunar throne-room confrontation holds up as a piece of staging, not just a technical demo.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <h2 style="font-size:.76rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.08em; color:var(--muted); font-family:-apple-system,sans-serif; font-weight:700; margin:0 0 20px; border:none;">Latest</h2>
  <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:36px 32px;">
    <article>
      <div style="border-radius:8px; overflow:hidden; aspect-ratio:16/9; margin-bottom:14px; background:var(--bg-elev);">
        <img src="/images/posters/echo-hunter-wide.webp" alt="Echo Hunter title card" style="width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover; display:block;" />
      </div>
      <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; margin-bottom:10px; font-size:.78rem; color:var(--muted);">
        <span style="display:inline-flex; align-items:center; background:var(--bg-elev); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:999px; padding:3px 11px; font-size:.68rem; font-weight:700; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.04em;">News</span>
        <time datetime="2025-06-02">Jun 2, 2025</time>
      </div>
      <h3 style="font-size:1.08rem; line-height:1.25; margin:0 0 .45em;">What Echo Hunter's SAG-AFTRA sign-off actually means</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--muted); line-height:1.55; margin:0; font-size:.86rem;">Echo Hunter was produced with explicit performer consent and guild sign-off for re-rendering a live performance with Arcana AI's video model — a template other AI productions using a real actor's likeness are likely to follow as the space matures. We break down what was agreed to, and what it doesn't cover.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <div style="border-radius:8px; overflow:hidden; aspect-ratio:16/9; margin-bottom:14px; background:var(--soft); display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; color:var(--muted); font-size:.85rem; font-weight:700; text-align:center; padding:10px;">Toys "R" Us × Sora</div>
      <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; margin-bottom:10px; font-size:.78rem; color:var(--muted);">
        <span style="display:inline-flex; align-items:center; background:var(--bg-elev); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:999px; padding:3px 11px; font-size:.68rem; font-weight:700; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.04em;">News</span>
        <time datetime="2024-05-10">May 10, 2024</time>
      </div>
      <h3 style="font-size:1.08rem; line-height:1.25; margin:0 0 .45em;">Toys "R" Us and the first wave of AI brand films</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--muted); line-height:1.55; margin:0; font-size:.86rem;">The Sora-produced Toys "R" Us spot was one of the first major brand commercials built with a text-to-video model, and it's aged into a useful reference point for how fast — and unevenly — the technology has moved since.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
